@* Tag's Overview, written by hand after Alert's: colors and variants, links, icons
   and sizes, removable filters (previewed in each mode). Accessibility and See also come from the
   doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A tag is a keyword, a category or a filter that's applied, and can be a link or removed. For a small status label or a count, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/badge">Badge</Anchor>; for choosing several values in a form, a <Anchor Href="docs/components/multi-select">MultiSelect</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Status and variants</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Status</Code> or <Code>Accent</Code> for the color and <Code>Variant</Code> for the weight: <Code>Soft</Code> (the default), <Code>Solid</Code> or <Code>Outline</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tag-variants" />

<Heading Level="2">Links, icons and sizes</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Href</Code> to make a tag a link, <Code>StartIcon</Code> for an icon and <Code>Size</Code> for 20, 24 or 28px tall.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tag-links-sizes" />

<Heading Level="2">Removable</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>RemoveHref</Code> for a remove link that works on any page, such as the current address without that filter, and <Code>OnRemove</Code> for C# on interactive ones.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tag-remove" />
<TextBlock>Give both, as here, when a tag may render in either: an interactive page uses <Code>OnRemove</Code>, and a static one the link. With only <Code>OnRemove</Code>, a static page shows no remove control at all. For a row of filters a <Anchor Href="docs/components/filter-form">FilterForm</Anchor> applies, build each <Code>RemoveHref</Code> with <Code>Navigation.GetUriWithQueryParameter</Code> so the rest of the address stays.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Its own words</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>RemoveLabel</Code> for the word before the label in the remove control's name ("Remove", as in "Remove Blazor"), or set it for the whole app as in <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Tag Label="Blazor" Href="/topics/blazor" />

        @* An applied filter: a link on static pages, C# on interactive ones. *@
        <Tag Label="Status: Paid" Status="Status.Success"
             RemoveHref="@Navigation.GetUriWithQueryParameter("status", (string?)null)"
             OnRemove="ClearStatus" />
        """;
}
